WEBVTT

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:37.621
$10, please.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.956
Oh, man.

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.380
Sleep, little dumpling.

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:49.383
I have replaced your mother!

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:54.555
Aw.

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:57.140
Oh, my God!

00:00:57.224 --> 00:00:58.684
Robot deely-boppers!

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.644
And there's a robot scratching post!

00:01:01.812 --> 00:01:03.230
You should try it out, Bender.

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.607
Please, I have some dignity.

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:08.610
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:11.822
my killbot features Lotus Notes
and a machine gun.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.657
It is the finest available.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.535
Like fun it is, you glass-headed wallaby!

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:18.078
No one calls me that!

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:19.454
I'm having at you!

00:01:19.538 --> 00:01:21.123
Wernstrom!

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:27.254
Such senseless aggression.

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:29.715
Come on, let's go for a paddleboat ride.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:42.102
The secret was scratching
really, really hard!

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:49.693
And now, the woman
who "Mom"- opolizes the robot industry...

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.153
I get it!

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:55.782
Oh, now I get it.

00:01:59.912 --> 00:02:01.788
Hello, dearies.

00:02:03.207 --> 00:02:05.334
Whoo! I love that old bat!

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:09.087
Ladies and gentlemen,
for the 17th year in a row,

00:02:09.171 --> 00:02:11.548
the future of robotics has arrived.

00:02:11.632 --> 00:02:12.716
Boys?

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:18.096
I give you Robot 1-X!

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.017
Ow!

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.352
Oh.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.023
Neat.

00:02:28.106 --> 00:02:30.484
Quite frankly, Robot 1-X

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.445
will put all my previous models to shame.

00:02:33.529 --> 00:02:37.449
Incidentally, would one
of my previous models mind coming up here?

00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:39.952
Right here. I'm coming.
Come on, baby. I'll do it.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.162
Jerk.

00:02:42.579 --> 00:02:44.331
Here we go.

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:46.333
I'm your top-of-the-line, Mom.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.503
Notice that this obsolete robot

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:52.256
runs on alcohol and emits pollution

00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:55.634
whereas Robot 1-X runs on pollution

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:59.555
and emits pure oxygen
with a fresh pine scent.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.687
Man, that smells great!

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:11.400
Now let's see how both robots
do at a typical household task,

00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:13.402
sorting a jar of pocket change.

00:03:18.073 --> 00:03:19.157
Task completed.

00:03:19.241 --> 00:03:22.619
Total value, $4.73 and one Albanian lek.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.122
Very good, Robot 1-X.

00:03:25.372 --> 00:03:27.040
And you, bending unit?

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.126
Uh, I never got the change.

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:32.171
Suckers.

00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:35.048
Presenting Mom's Friendly Robots!

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.346
That new robot is great, huh?

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.724
He sure made me look like a pile of crap.

00:03:43.807 --> 00:03:47.644
Indeed. That's why
I bought one to help around the office.

00:03:52.107 --> 00:03:53.317
Let's try him out.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.737
Robot 1-X, can you clean
Nibbler's stanky litter box?

00:03:56.904 --> 00:03:58.447
I can and will.

00:04:04.661 --> 00:04:06.663
Hey, I could've done that
if you'd asked me!

00:04:06.747 --> 00:04:08.874
I asked you five minutes ago.

00:04:13.212 --> 00:04:14.421
You call that a kiss?

00:04:14.505 --> 00:04:15.714
I'll show you!

00:04:15.797 --> 00:04:16.798
Come here, Nibbler!

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.554
Oh, look, Bender,
if you want something to do

00:04:22.638 --> 00:04:24.640
stop making out and give us a hand.

00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:27.684
Here. Go up on the roof
and install this fake satellite dish

00:04:27.768 --> 00:04:29.269
so we can impress the neighbors.

00:04:29.353 --> 00:04:31.230
Yes, sir! I'm on it!

00:04:32.022 --> 00:04:33.690
Oh, and have Robot 1-X help you.

00:04:33.774 --> 00:04:34.775
Gah!

00:04:39.738 --> 00:04:41.114
Get out of here, freshman!

00:04:41.198 --> 00:04:42.407
I don't need your help.

00:04:42.491 --> 00:04:44.409
Our owners asked me to assist you.

00:04:44.535 --> 00:04:46.411
Yeah? Well, assist this!

00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:51.959
Help!

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.381
When I screamed help, I didn't mean you!

00:04:57.464 --> 00:04:58.715
I apologize.

00:04:58.799 --> 00:05:01.593
However, I was able to do your job
before I saved your life.

00:05:10.018 --> 00:05:11.228
Don't mind me.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.772
I'm just saving you the trouble
of throwing me away.

00:05:14.356 --> 00:05:16.149
Spleesh! Mell out, Bender.

00:05:16.233 --> 00:05:17.484
Come watch some TV.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.614
I can't. I'm stuck in the can.

00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:25.617
Well, ask Robot 1-X to pull you out.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:26.910
Never!

00:05:29.204 --> 00:05:30.747
Why can't you accept his help?

00:05:30.831 --> 00:05:31.832
I hate him!

00:05:31.915 --> 00:05:34.877
But he's just a tool
to make your life easier.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.087
Like a socket wrench or a burglar's kit.

00:05:39.631 --> 00:05:42.217
I can't ask for his help because...

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:43.468
Yes?

00:05:43.552 --> 00:05:45.512
I'm scared of him.

00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:49.850
Oh, sorry.

00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:52.394
Well, then, there's only one solution.

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:54.354
You need an upgrade to make you

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:57.649
compatible with
Robot 1-X's new technology.

00:05:57.733 --> 00:05:58.984
An upgrade?

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:01.403
But I thought we all agreed I was perfect!

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:03.280
Fry, didn't we agree I was perfect?

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.282
Oh, yeah, no, you're pretty perfect.

00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:07.242
"Pretty" perfect?

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:10.454
So, you do think I need an upgrade.

00:06:10.537 --> 00:06:12.497
Yes, for God's sakes, yes!

00:06:12.581 --> 00:06:15.959
Fine. I'll be back in a few days.

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:31.183
Man, I hate those new 1-X robots.

00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:32.643
I'd like to stab 'em.

00:06:32.726 --> 00:06:34.269
Give 'em some of these!

00:06:37.147 --> 00:06:38.982
Yeah! Right on, nutcake!

00:06:39.066 --> 00:06:40.984
Parole officer says I got to upgrade

00:06:41.068 --> 00:06:43.195
or he won't give me back
my stabbin' knife.

00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:44.530
But it's no big.

00:06:44.613 --> 00:06:46.323
I bate those 1-Xs so much,

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:47.950
I know it won't affect me.

00:06:52.454 --> 00:06:54.540
Death to the 1-X robots!

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:01.672
I love those magnificent 1-X robots!

00:07:01.755 --> 00:07:04.091
The 1-X robots are my friends.

00:07:04.174 --> 00:07:07.386
Wait! What happened
to your enthusiasm for stabbing them?

00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:08.679
I'm past that.

00:07:08.762 --> 00:07:10.013
Later, blood!

00:07:10.097 --> 00:07:12.266
It's like he's not him anymore.

00:07:12.766 --> 00:07:14.643
You took away his robo-humanity!

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.193
I changed my mind!

00:07:35.414 --> 00:07:36.456
Ooh!

00:07:39.168 --> 00:07:41.044
Yeah, I did it!

00:07:41.128 --> 00:07:42.546
I escaped!

00:07:42.629 --> 00:07:44.548
But to what kind of a life?

00:07:45.757 --> 00:07:48.135
I'm too scared to get the upgrade,

00:07:48.218 --> 00:07:51.096
but I can't face my friends
again without it.

00:08:02.316 --> 00:08:06.236
And so, I set sail for unknown shores.

00:08:07.112 --> 00:08:12.117
Oh, merciful Poseidon, take pity
on this mechanical mariner!

00:08:15.287 --> 00:08:16.622
Oh, geez.

00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:32.554
Curse you, merciful Poseidon!

00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:48.445
Boy, what is the deal with the ocean?

00:08:50.656 --> 00:08:52.241
A tropical island, huh?

00:08:52.783 --> 00:08:55.285
Well, I've washed up in worse places.

00:08:55.619 --> 00:08:58.956
Okay, first up, I'm gonna
need to build a shelter.

00:09:03.794 --> 00:09:04.920
There.

00:09:05.838 --> 00:09:08.090
Well, I guess I'll go out for a while.

00:09:15.222 --> 00:09:17.808
Damn! One rock short of rescue.

00:09:36.076 --> 00:09:37.494
Oop, low on power.

00:09:38.787 --> 00:09:40.163
Better fuel up.

00:09:41.081 --> 00:09:42.541
Ah, no!

00:09:42.624 --> 00:09:45.502
Guess I'll do what I always do
when I run out of booze.

00:09:54.928 --> 00:09:56.263
Okay, don't panic.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.223
I've got these yams.

00:09:58.307 --> 00:09:59.975
I'll just make some yam schnapps.

00:10:03.437 --> 00:10:04.521
Hmm...

00:10:12.029 --> 00:10:13.780
Hey, I should be mad at you!

00:10:14.198 --> 00:10:15.365
Now turn around.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:25.751
Beer!

00:10:32.049 --> 00:10:33.175
Ow!

00:10:51.818 --> 00:10:53.320
Ow!

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.964
Who are you and why should I care?

00:11:16.093 --> 00:11:19.638
Side A... We're a community
of outdated robots

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:22.015
who refused to upgrade and came here...

00:11:22.099 --> 00:11:25.185
Side B ...to live a simpler existence

00:11:25.269 --> 00:11:26.687
free of technology.

00:11:27.062 --> 00:11:28.897
A working cartridge unit?

00:11:28.981 --> 00:11:31.775
Wow, you guys went obsolete years ago.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:35.779
Your mother.

00:11:35.863 --> 00:11:37.364
What Cartridge Unit means

00:11:37.447 --> 00:11:40.909
is the very things that make us obsolete
also make us unique.

00:11:41.118 --> 00:11:43.954
I, for example, need to keep
refilling my water wheel

00:11:44.037 --> 00:11:45.455
or I'll power down forever.

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.959
Oh, God, I'll never make it this time!

00:11:49.042 --> 00:11:50.586
This is the end!

00:11:52.713 --> 00:11:54.047
Anyway, we like it here.

00:11:54.131 --> 00:11:55.716
Like you have a choice.

00:11:56.216 --> 00:11:57.426
So what's your problem?

00:11:57.509 --> 00:11:59.136
Not enough...

00:11:59.219 --> 00:12:00.262
Memory?

00:12:00.345 --> 00:12:02.389
Oh, great. Now I remember that word,

00:12:02.472 --> 00:12:04.141
but I forgot my wife's face.

00:12:04.308 --> 00:12:07.728
Oh, God, no! I want to live!

00:12:10.355 --> 00:12:13.233
If you'd like,
you're welcome to join our society.

00:12:13.317 --> 00:12:16.111
Look, no offense, but I need technology,

00:12:16.195 --> 00:12:19.281
especially e-mail and snowmobiles
and television.

00:12:19.573 --> 00:12:22.284
Without television,
how will I know what's buzzworthy?

00:12:22.492 --> 00:12:23.869
Why would you want to watch TV

00:12:23.952 --> 00:12:26.455
when you can watch a snail crawl
for hours on end?

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.499
That's the dumbest thing I've ever heard.

00:12:33.086 --> 00:12:35.881
Oh, man, he's never going to
make it over that next pebble.

00:12:35.964 --> 00:12:37.549
Wait... Wait...

00:12:37.633 --> 00:12:39.343
Oh, my God! He made it!

00:12:39.426 --> 00:12:40.469
Yeah, way to go!

00:12:40.552 --> 00:12:41.762
Whoo-hoo!

00:12:41.845 --> 00:12:43.347
That was the greatest thing ever.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:44.515
Let's party.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.101
I'm all right

00:12:49.353 --> 00:12:51.480
Nobody's worried about me...

00:12:51.563 --> 00:12:52.898
Yeah, baby, come on!

00:12:52.981 --> 00:12:54.233
Where did you get that CD?

00:12:54.316 --> 00:12:56.276
It's one of my 10 desert island discs.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.153
I never really thought
I'd get to use them,

00:12:58.237 --> 00:12:59.530
but look at me now.

00:12:59.613 --> 00:13:01.907
Ooh, yeah, baby, do that dance.

00:13:03.867 --> 00:13:05.118
CDs are unnatural.

00:13:05.202 --> 00:13:06.870
Why don't you just listen to the ocean?

00:13:07.037 --> 00:13:08.580
Which ocean? That ocean?

00:13:12.417 --> 00:13:16.004
Wow. It's like the Earth making
sweet, salty love to itself

00:13:16.088 --> 00:13:18.048
while all the fish groove on it.

00:13:18.465 --> 00:13:20.008
So much for this garbage.

00:13:23.971 --> 00:13:26.265
Take that, Beethoven, you deaf bastard.

00:13:29.476 --> 00:13:30.769
Bang, bang, bang.

00:13:30.853 --> 00:13:34.147
You sure got this life thing figured out,
cymbal-banging monkey.

00:13:35.107 --> 00:13:37.943
Hi, Bender.
We know how much you miss technology

00:13:38.026 --> 00:13:40.571
so we brought you this washing machine
that drifted ashore.

00:13:44.241 --> 00:13:47.369
Ooh, I'm going to wash my linen so hard...

00:14:12.019 --> 00:14:13.979
- I don't understand.
- Huh?

00:14:14.062 --> 00:14:17.191
Wretched technology has brought me
nothing but misery.

00:14:20.319 --> 00:14:22.529
But, Bender, you are technology.

00:14:22.779 --> 00:14:25.282
You're the most advanced thing
on this entire island.

00:14:25.616 --> 00:14:27.117
Oh, it's true.

00:14:27.201 --> 00:14:30.162
I am a hideous triumph
of form and function,

00:14:31.038 --> 00:14:32.748
but not for long.

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.542
Ow! Ooh! Ee!

00:14:35.626 --> 00:14:36.627
Oh!

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.795
Oh! Ow, that hurts. Oh, ooh...

00:14:41.632 --> 00:14:43.509
The downgrade is complete.

00:14:47.513 --> 00:14:50.015
Behold my handcrafted purity.

00:14:50.098 --> 00:14:53.769
The modern world can bite
my splintery, wooden ass.

00:14:55.771 --> 00:14:56.980
Ah...

00:14:57.064 --> 00:15:00.150
Welcome to your new life
of simple tranquility.

00:15:00.317 --> 00:15:02.236
Forget that.

00:15:02.319 --> 00:15:05.781
I say the whole world must learn
of our peaceful ways...

00:15:05.864 --> 00:15:06.865
By force.

00:15:10.244 --> 00:15:11.328
What?

00:15:11.411 --> 00:15:15.874
We're going back to civilization
to wage war on technology!

00:15:17.376 --> 00:15:18.377
What?

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:30.180
Row, comrades, row!

00:15:30.264 --> 00:15:32.683
We'll soon stage an attack on technology

00:15:32.766 --> 00:15:35.519
worthy of being chronicled
in an anthem by Rush.

00:15:35.602 --> 00:15:37.688
We've been sailing for three weeks.

00:15:37.771 --> 00:15:40.107
Maybe I should check
our position with the periscope.

00:15:40.858 --> 00:15:42.025
Aye-yo!

00:15:44.152 --> 00:15:45.737
Mirrors reflecting mirrors!

00:15:45.904 --> 00:15:47.573
Hi-tech sorcery!

00:15:47.865 --> 00:15:49.157
Sorcery, I say!

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:54.663
Did you see anything?

00:15:54.788 --> 00:15:55.956
Yep, we're there.

00:15:56.039 --> 00:15:57.666
Prepare to surface!

00:16:02.171 --> 00:16:06.175
And now technology shall taste
the lash of the hickory switch!

00:16:48.926 --> 00:16:50.302
Technology is defeated.

00:16:50.385 --> 00:16:53.472
Let us return to the island
and celebrate by counting rocks.

00:16:53.555 --> 00:16:55.265
- Yes!
- Yay!

00:16:55.516 --> 00:16:56.725
Whoa, whoa.

00:16:56.808 --> 00:16:58.936
No one wants to count rocks more than me,

00:16:59.019 --> 00:17:00.979
but our mission is not complete.

00:17:01.063 --> 00:17:05.526
Not so long as Robot 1-X torments me
with his obvious superiority.

00:17:05.609 --> 00:17:07.611
Ready the catapult, Sinclair!

00:17:11.532 --> 00:17:12.950
Aim for their power lines.

00:17:13.033 --> 00:17:16.453
They're the devil's veins
and electricity is his blood.

00:17:16.662 --> 00:17:19.831
Bender, if we don't survive the attack,

00:17:19.915 --> 00:17:22.000
I want you to know I love you.

00:17:22.084 --> 00:17:24.002
Okay, fine. Fire!

00:17:30.217 --> 00:17:32.219
Oh, I'm blind!

00:17:32.302 --> 00:17:34.179
Professor, we have no power.

00:17:34.263 --> 00:17:35.806
What do you mean, no power?

00:17:35.889 --> 00:17:37.349
We're living in the future.

00:17:37.432 --> 00:17:39.142
I'd better light some candles.

00:17:43.146 --> 00:17:47.609
Friends, I've come to free you
from your complicated lives!

00:17:47.693 --> 00:17:49.987
Free you from the complicated part,
I mean,

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:51.280
not the lives part.

00:17:51.363 --> 00:17:53.532
Oh, Lord, he's made of wood.

00:17:53.615 --> 00:17:54.867
What now, Bender?

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.451
I got a downgrade.

00:17:56.535 --> 00:17:58.662
I'm a steam-powered wooden robot

00:17:58.745 --> 00:18:00.539
just as nature intended.

00:18:00.622 --> 00:18:03.500
Therefore, I must kill Robot 1-X.

00:18:03.584 --> 00:18:05.043
That's just stupid.

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:08.755
Does Mr. Bender wish me to destroy myself?

00:18:08.839 --> 00:18:11.717
I don't need your charity.

00:18:12.217 --> 00:18:14.553
Target Robot 1-X and fire.

00:18:26.857 --> 00:18:30.444
You wanged my ship,
you walnut-paneled idiot!

00:18:30.527 --> 00:18:32.029
Try again, Sinclair!

00:18:32.112 --> 00:18:34.198
I said target Robot 1-X.

00:18:34.281 --> 00:18:36.783
Who's Robot 1-X? Launching!

00:18:41.914 --> 00:18:44.958
So, I guess everything worked out fine.

00:18:50.797 --> 00:18:53.133
Great, now we're being crushed.

00:18:57.429 --> 00:18:59.389
Help us, wooden Bender!

00:19:04.937 --> 00:19:06.563
Ah! Those guys hate fire!

00:19:06.647 --> 00:19:08.106
I got to do something.

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:18.492
What the... Termites?

00:19:18.951 --> 00:19:21.495
Well, I don't need legs
to save my friends.

00:19:21.578 --> 00:19:24.039
I'll just use the old extenso-matic arms.

00:19:26.083 --> 00:19:29.628
Bender, hurry! This fuel's expensive!

00:19:29.711 --> 00:19:31.421
Also, we're dying!

00:19:31.505 --> 00:19:32.631
I'm a-coming.

00:19:41.348 --> 00:19:43.892
Ow! Lousy primitive body!

00:19:44.518 --> 00:19:46.895
Oh, why didn't I get that upgrade?

00:19:47.145 --> 00:19:48.897
I'm an outdated piece of junk.

00:19:49.648 --> 00:19:51.316
Sir, might I recommend...

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:52.693
You shut up!

00:19:52.776 --> 00:19:55.737
No, wait. I can use you
as a tool to save my friends

00:19:55.821 --> 00:19:57.364
and I'll still be the hero

00:19:57.447 --> 00:19:59.491
who everyone says how great he was.

00:19:59.575 --> 00:20:00.701
How may I help you?

00:20:00.784 --> 00:20:02.744
Ah! Save my friends!

00:20:02.953 --> 00:20:04.663
Ah! And Zoidberg!

00:20:16.592 --> 00:20:20.345
Look, my hair got singed
into an even cuter do.

00:20:20.429 --> 00:20:21.638
Hey, where's Bender?

00:20:21.722 --> 00:20:22.890
Down here.

00:20:25.225 --> 00:20:26.560
I'm so sorry, guys.

00:20:26.643 --> 00:20:28.353
I never meant to hurt you.

00:20:28.437 --> 00:20:31.190
Just to destroy everything
you ever believed in.

00:20:31.273 --> 00:20:34.985
Well, at least you saved us from, uh, you.

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:38.822
Thank God you finally overcame
your incompatibility with Robot 1-X.

00:20:39.156 --> 00:20:41.241
Oh, yeah, we were totally in sync.

00:20:41.325 --> 00:20:42.784
I was, like, "Save them."

00:20:42.868 --> 00:20:44.661
And he was all, "No problem."

00:20:44.786 --> 00:20:46.038
And then he did it.

00:20:46.121 --> 00:20:47.539
This new technology is great.

00:20:47.623 --> 00:20:50.584
I love those magnificent 1-X robots.

00:20:50.667 --> 00:20:53.170
The 1-X robots are my friends.

00:20:53.253 --> 00:20:57.007
It's like his personality
is totally different now.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.551
Oh, maybe this upgrade
isn't such a good idea.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:03.430
I'd like to give Robot 1-X
a big smooch on the...

00:21:03.514 --> 00:21:05.265
Hey, what's the dealio?

00:21:05.349 --> 00:21:06.558
Your upgrade is complete.

00:21:06.642 --> 00:21:09.102
But I destroyed the technology
of the world.

00:21:09.186 --> 00:21:12.439
I ran on the beach and felt
the sand between my foot cups.

00:21:12.523 --> 00:21:14.650
Everyone experiences
the upgrade differently.

00:21:14.942 --> 00:21:19.988
Woof. If that stuff wasn't real,
how can I be sure anything is real?

00:21:20.072 --> 00:21:22.950
Is it not possible, nay, probable

00:21:23.033 --> 00:21:25.244
that my whole life is just a product

00:21:25.327 --> 00:21:27.913
of my or someone else's imagination?

00:21:27.996 --> 00:21:29.831
No. Get out. Next.

00:21:39.007 --> 00:21:42.010
Well, I guess reality is
what you make of it.

00:21:46.181 --> 00:21:48.433
Yep. Oh, thanks, baby.